    "long_instructions": "### **Game HUD**\r\n\r\n#### **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. **Review the example:** Look at the completed button. Notice how the function is written as a named arrow function and how it is connected using `addEventListener`.\r\n\r\n2. Read a function description for another button in `prompt.md`.\r\n\r\n3. Highlight the button description, select **Add to AI Tutor Chat**, and ask the AI to write a named arrow function that matches the description.\r\n\r\n4. Create an event handler using `addEventListener(\"click\", functionName)` and add your function.\r\n\r\n5. Click the button and confirm that it works as expected.\r\n\r\n6. Complete the same steps for the remaining buttons.",
    "display_name": "Game HUD",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <title>L4 — Game HUD</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  <script defer src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>Game HUD</h1>\n  <p>Track health and power with simple button actions.</p>\n\n  <p>\n    Health: <span id=\"healthDisplay\">100</span>\n    &nbsp;&nbsp;\n    Power: <span id=\"powerDisplay\">1</span>\n  </p>\n\n  <p id=\"output\">Ready.</p>\n\n  <h2>Actions</h2>\n  <button id=\"powerUpButton\">Power Up</button>\n  <button id=\"loseHealthButton\">Lose 10 Health</button>\n  <button id=\"applyPowerButton\">Apply Power</button>\n  <button id=\"resetButton\">Reset</button>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "body {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  background: #f5f7ff;\n  text-align: center;\n  padding: 24px 12px;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  margin: 10px 0;\n}\n\nh2 {\n  margin-top: 24px;\n}\n\np {\n  margin: 8px 0;\n}\n\n#healthDisplay,\n#powerDisplay {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding: 4px 10px;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  margin-left: 6px;\n}\n\n#healthDisplay {\n  background: #fee2e2;\n  color: #991b1b;\n}\n\n#powerDisplay {\n  background: #ede9fe;\n  color: #5b21b6;\n}\n\n#output {\n  margin: 16px auto;\n  max-width: 400px;\n  min-height: 30px;\n  padding: 10px;\n  border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  background: #fbfdff;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  display: inline-block;\n  margin: 6px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\n}\n\n#powerUpButton {\n  background: #ddd6fe;\n  border-color: #c4b5fd;\n  color: #5b21b6;\n}\n\n#loseHealthButton {\n  background: #fee2e2;\n  border-color: #fecaca;\n  color: #b91c1c;\n}\n\n#applyPowerButton {\n  background: #dbeafe;\n  border-color: #93c5fd;\n  color: #1e3a8a;\n}\n\n#resetButton {\n  background: #f3f4f6;\n  border-color: #d1d5db;\n  color: #374151;\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  opacity: 0.9;\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "const powerUpButton = document.getElementById(\"powerUpButton\");\n\nconst powerDisplay = document.getElementById(\"powerDisplay\");\nconst output = document.getElementById(\"output\");\n\nlet power = 1;\n\nconst powerUp = () => {\n  power = power * 2;\n\n  powerDisplay.textContent = power;\n  output.textContent = \"Power increased.\";\n};\n\npowerUpButton.addEventListener(\"click\", powerUp);",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "prompt.md",
          "contents": "## Power Up Button\nName of the button: Power Up\nEvent type: click\nWhat the button should do: increase the power\nWhat on the page changes: the power number and the message\n\n\n## Lose Health Button\nName of the button: Lose Health\nEvent type: click\nWhat the button should do: decrease the health\nWhat on the page changes: the health number and the message\n\n\n## Apply Power Button\nName of the button: Apply Power\nEvent type: click\nWhat the button should do: apply the power to the health\nWhat on the page changes: the health number and the message\n\n\n## Reset Button\nName of the button: Reset\nEvent type: click\nWhat the button should do: reset health and power to starting values\nWhat on the page changes: the health number, the power number, and the message\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "4",
        "3"
      ]
    },
